WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.370
-Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.371
has promised
a scorched-earth Senate

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.173
if Democrats change
the filibuster

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.309
to pass sweeping and urgently
needed democracy reforms

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.645
as Republicans
across the country unleash

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.281
a tidal wave of draconian new
voting restrictions

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.950
motivated by the big lie

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.452
that Donald Trump was the real
winner of the 2020 election.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.788
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:25.624
♪♪

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:27.627
Our democracy
as currently constituted

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.628
is simply not
a level playing field.

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:32.131
In fact, it's arguably never
been a level playing field.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.467
It's heavily tilted
toward a minority of voters

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.469
that are predominantly
white and rural,

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.806
thanks in large part to
anti-majoritarian institutions

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.474
like the Electoral College
and the Senate.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:45.311
Just consider that right now the
Senate is evenly split 50/50

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.313
and yet the 50 Senate Democrats

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.982
represent nearly 42 million
more Americans

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.483
than the 50 Senate Republicans.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:52.819
For example, Wyoming,

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.421
with a population of about
580,000 people,

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:56.589
has two senators,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.758
and New York also has
two senators,

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.427
even though there are
580,000 people

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.429
just on my co-op board,

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.598
which is why I'm still
waiting on approval

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.601
for the welcome mat
I bought in 2002.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.437
Think about that.
42 million more Americans.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.038
That's just an insane fact.

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:17.210
Like, if every touchdown the
Jets scored was worth 42 points,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.278
they wouldn't make the playoffs,

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.115 line:0%
but they'd be in more
close games.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.583
I mean, just consider the scope
of how heavily tilted

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.919
our democratic institutions are
toward Republicans.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.754
They've only won
the popular vote once

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.256
in the last 32 years,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.226
yet they've appointed a majority
of Supreme Court justices.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:37.062
They've lost the popular vote
by nearly 3 million in 2016,

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:40.399
lost the House by the largest
margin since Watergate in 2018,

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.734
lost two Senate seats

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.569
in historically red Georgia
this year,

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.239
and yet Mitch McConnell still
basically gets a veto

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.207
over what the Senate can
or cannot pass.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.710
The only way the Senate can
get anything done right now

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.045
is through a process called
budget reconciliation,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.748
which has more rules than
a Manhattan parking sign.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.125
Seriously, what is that?

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.127
I stop in to grab
a prescription, I get a ticket,

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.462
but this van has actual weeds

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:13.098
growing up through
the wheel wells? Alright.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:15.368
The Democrats were able to pass
their massively popular

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.369
COVID relief bill
through reconciliation,

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.539
but thanks to
the Senate parliamentarian

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.041
and a bunch of absurd rules
no one understands,

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.544
they had to drop their proposal
for a $15 minimum wage.

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:28.547
Trying to pass legislation
through budget reconciliation

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.883
is like trying to play some
obscure board game

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.885
your most annoying friend
brought back from Europe.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:33.986
It's called Viking Quest.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:35.821
You role-play as
a Nordic sea commander

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:37.824
searching for gold coins
buried in trenches.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.993
Whenever you search a trench,
you get an action card,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.228
which adds to your skill table,
allowing to you trade for cargo

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.731
which you can use to score
victory points.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.733
And whoever scores
the most victory points

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.068
gets to leave board game night
and go home.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.736
It's from the same company
that makes Ocean Master.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.872
They also make NyQuill,
with two L's.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.039
Keeps you up.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.374
So, the deck is already stacked

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.076
heavily in
the Republicans' favor.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.580
And yet because they still got
swamped in the 2020 elections,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.915
they're trying to make it even
harder for Americans to vote.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.584
State election officials across
the country expanded

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:08.587
mail and early voting in 2020
because of the pandemic.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:11.591
And by the way, if you judge
the health of a democracy

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.092
not by the results
but by how many people voted,

00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:15.494
it was a huge success.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.697
Voter fraud was
virtually nonexistent,

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.198
as has been the case
for decades,

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.467
even as turnout was the highest
in over a century.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.269
You know how everyone's
always complaining

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.937
about low voter turnout
in America?

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.605
2020 showed us how to fix it.

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:27.940
Just make voting easier.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.276
Let people vote at their
convenience, either in person

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.278
or by dropping off a ballot
in the mail.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.280
Voting should take
a few minutes, tops.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.614
Everything else has gotten
easier in America.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:36.783
Why not voting?

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.950
Remember when your mom
used to have to call

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.418
the Mexican restaurant
to order delivery?

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.254
Now there are a million apps,

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.922
which is great because
you don't have to hear her

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.590
pronounce the L's
in "quesadilla."

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.091
"I'd like two quesa-dill-a

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:47.760
with guac-ah-ma-lay."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.395
And yet to register to vote,

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.230
you have to bring
like three forms of I.D.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.732
to the county registrar

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.568
in some government building
you've never even seen before

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:58.404
that looks like the crawl space
from "Being John Malkovich."

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.906
And it shouldn't be on Tuesday,
our [bleep] day.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.909
Now, some may argue that Monday
is worse, but would you

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.978
prefer Memorial Day
to fall on a Tuesday?

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.979
You wouldn't,
because Tuesday's [bleep]

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:08.647
If you said to a friend,
"We should get dinner soon"

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:09.948
and they said,
"How about Tuesday?"

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:11.650
you'd say, "How about
you [bleep] right off?"

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:12.985
And don't start on Wednesday.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.488
I'd trade a hundred Tuesdays
for one Wednesday.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.658
Hump day?
Tuesday is chump day!

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.594
Anyway, the point is voting
should be as easy as possible

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.262
and everyone should
automatically be enrolled

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:25.265
or have the ability to enroll
on election day.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.932
Of course, if Republicans
had their way,

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.934
there'd be one ballot box
in every state,

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.337
it would be open for three hours
from 2:00 to 5:00 a.m.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.439
on National
We're-Not-Telling-You Day,

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.541
and it would be at the end
of a spooky corn maze.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:36.709
Ooh! No, thanks.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.378
I'll take my chances
with President Ivanka.

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.715
And sure enough, GOP state
legislators across the country

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.717
have responded to
their thumping in 2020

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.385
by adopting new policies

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.953
that appeal to a majority
of Americans --

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:51.457
Sorry! I mean, unleashing
an unprecedented tidal wave

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.959
of voter suppression laws.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.060
-Across 43 states,

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.397
more than 250 new voting laws
have been proposed.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.633
They include efforts
that would limit mail-in

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.703
and early in-person voting,
as well as election day voting,

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.705
with constraints such as
stricter I.D. requirements,

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.040
limited voting hours,

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.876
and narrower qualifications
for absentee ballots.

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:14.046
-My God. 250 laws in 43 states?

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.448
Republicans are really not
being subtle about it.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:17.950
I mean, wouldn't it be easier
and more honest

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.551
to propose just one bill

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.888
that would replace every ballot
in a Democratic precinct

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.155
with a shredder?

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:24.957
You know, I have a sinking
feeling when I said that,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.625
Mitch McConnell sat up in bed
and chuckled

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.627
like a battery-powered
Halloween doll.

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:31.430
[As McConnell]
[ Chuckles ] I like that idea.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.933
[ Slow, halting chuckle ]

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.936
Back to bed.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.604
[Normal voice] All this
is motivated, of course,

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.273
by the Big Lie,
the deranged conspiracy theory

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.276
pushed by Donald Trump
and his supporters

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.277
that he was somehow robbed
of the election

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.746
by widespread voter fraud --
which, again, did not exist.

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:50.582
In fact, on Tuesday,
he dispensed with any pretense

00:05:50.582 --> 00:05:52.251
about so-called
election integrity

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.421
and said straight-up on Fox News
that the Supreme Court

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.489
should have stolen the election
for him.

00:05:57.489 --> 00:06:00.826
-Our Supreme Court and our
courts didn't have the courage

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.696
to overturn elections that
should have been overturned.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.465
-I love when Trump gets tired
of a schtick

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.133
and just says the thing
he wants to say.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.135
It's like when you're in
hour six of a break-up talk

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.838
and you finally say, "Because
you breathe weird, okay?

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:14.506
You're a weird breather.

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:16.008
And that's a problem
because you do it --

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.843
as you should -- constantly."

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.411
Republicans are out there
pretending

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:20.980
these voter suppression laws
are about

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.783
so-called election integrity and
restoring faith in democracy,

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.884
and Trump just
blurts out the truth.

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:28.220
He's the friend who goes
with you to buy weed

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.889
and as soon as you say you got
the stuff, he says,

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.324
[as Trump]
"But not just any stuff.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:33.459
The marijuana stuff.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:36.529
Sorry!
The illegal marijuana stuff.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:39.031
Also known as Mary Jane.
Nasty woman.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.200
Mary Jane, always nice to me.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.369
I remember, she and I once
spent an evening

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.204
watching "The Wizard of Oz"

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.205
synced up with
"Dark Side of the Moon."

00:06:47.205 --> 00:06:48.974
Not my favorite
Pink Floyd album.

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:50.809
That would be "The Wall"!

00:06:50.809 --> 00:06:52.311
We love "The Wall," don't we?

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.979
An album they recorded,

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.482
but Mexico paid for.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.317
I should tell you guys,

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:01.487
I'm already pretty high.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:04.157
Does my --
My voice is weird.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:07.160
Weird.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.929
I've never listened to it."

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.430
[Normal voice] That's what
this is really all about.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.865
Their initial plan was to have

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:15.434
the court steal the election
for them, but that didn't work

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:18.804
because Biden won by too much
in too many states.

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.806
So now they're on to
their fallback plan --

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.975
passing a flurry
of new voting restrictions

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.710
to help them steal
the next election.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.212
Texas is the latest state
to join in

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:29.748
with a slate of proposed bills
that would, among other things,

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:31.917
take some of the most
popular voting methods

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.253
and either eliminate them
entirely

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:36.322
or make fewer people eligible
for them.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:39.558
-Texas is now the latest state
to see Republicans introduce

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:43.062
a flurry of bills that could
make it even harder to vote.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.898
-Texas Republicans are calling
for measures that would impose

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.033
new limits on early voting hours

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:50.702
and added requirements
on mail voting.

00:07:50.702 --> 00:07:53.772
Some of the legislation appears
to be aimed at Harris County,

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:56.442
a Democratic stronghold
and home to Houston,

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:59.111
which saw a surge in turnout
last year

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:01.514
after the county implemented
methods during the pandemic

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:04.683
such as 24-hour and
drive-through voting sites.

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:07.186
-That's right, Texas wants
to ban drive-through voting.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.854
How can you be against
drive-through voting?

00:08:08.854 --> 00:08:11.457
It combines the two most
American things --

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.392
democracy and drive-throughs.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.460
Personally, if you ask me,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.494
everything should be
drive-through.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.496
The pandemic has been
a nightmare,

00:08:17.496 --> 00:08:18.664
but one thing it's taught me is

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.499
I love not having to
get out of my car.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:21.833
I had dental surgery last week.

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.136
I just left the engine running.

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.972
Of course, the hardest...

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:27.473
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.276
I mean, I was there, but it's
jarring to see a photo of it.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:33.612
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.612 --> 00:08:35.681
Of course, the hardest part
of drive-through voting

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.149
is making sure
they hear you right.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:38.750
"Yeah, I'd like to vote
for Joe Biden."

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.220
"So, one Doritos Locos
taco supreme --"

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.222
"No, I said I want to vote
for Joe Biden."

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.890
"So, you want
the Crunch Wrap supreme?"

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.091
"No, I want -- Wait.

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:50.395
What-- What's in
the Crunch Wrap supreme?"

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:52.865
Another provision floated by
Texas Republicans would

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:55.467
shrink the period when voters
could return mail ballots,

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:58.570
while another bill would ask
voters to mail back photocopies

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.774
of their driver's licenses or
other qualifying identification

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.442
with their mail ballots.
And that makes sense because

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.444
if there's one thing
every American has,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.279
it's a copy machine at home.

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:09.281
We keep ours in the kids' room.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.650
And by the way, it won't shock
to you learn that none of this

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.819
is supported by any evidence
of actual voter fraud,

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:15.487
which, again, is
virtually nonexistent.

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:18.190
Trump tried to argue that there
was voter fraud in court

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.591
and he lost 60 times.

00:09:19.591 --> 00:09:23.095
In fact, Texas Attorney General
Ken Paxton's office

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:25.931
spent 22,000 hours
looking for voter fraud

00:09:25.931 --> 00:09:27.432
and uncovered just 16 cases

00:09:27.432 --> 00:09:29.802
of false addresses
on registration forms.

00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:31.304
22,000 hours.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:33.406
According to Malcolm Gladwell,
that's enough time to become

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:35.707
a concert cellist
and a pool shark

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:37.376
and get a decent start

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.378
on becoming a roller dance
instructor.

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.046
Texas is just the latest state
to jump on

00:09:41.046 --> 00:09:42.347
the anti-voting bandwagon.

00:09:42.347 --> 00:09:43.749
The same thing is happening
in Georgia,

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.951
where Trump desperately tried
to steal the state's votes

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.854
after losing to Biden last year.
The state GOP has unleashed

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:51.189
a flurry of draconian
anti-voting restrictions

00:09:51.189 --> 00:09:53.158
on everything from mail voting
to early voting

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:56.161
to Sunday voting to offering
voters snacks and water --

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:57.930
restrictions that are designed

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.664
to target Black voters
in particular,

00:09:59.664 --> 00:10:02.000
as Georgia Senator
Raphael Warnock pointed out

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.168
on Wednesday.

00:10:03.168 --> 00:10:05.003
-There is a move to ban
line warming.

00:10:05.003 --> 00:10:08.006
And what that is is where
volunteers will provide water,

00:10:08.006 --> 00:10:10.843
some snacks, even chairs to
voters that are standing in line

00:10:10.843 --> 00:10:11.877
for a long time.

00:10:11.877 --> 00:10:17.550
-They're the ones
making the lines longer.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:22.555
Through these draconian actions.

00:10:22.555 --> 00:10:25.224
And then they want
to make it a crime

00:10:25.224 --> 00:10:27.960
to bring Grandma some water
while she's waiting in a line

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.795
that they're making longer.
-That's right.

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:32.465
Republicans want to make it
a crime to give Grandma water.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.800
In fairness,
none of their old dudes

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.301
seem to drink any water.

00:10:36.301 --> 00:10:38.070
That's why they look like
dried apple dolls.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.105
All you have to do is pour
some water on Rudy

00:10:40.105 --> 00:10:43.809
and he'd immediately sprout hair
like a Chia Pet.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.644
[ Laughter ]

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:47.646
[As Giuliani] All this time,
I was using gutter water.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:49.815
It turns out,
I just need a drink.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:51.750
[Normal voice] Warnock delivered
an impassioned speech.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.552
in favor of sweeping
voting reforms

00:10:53.552 --> 00:10:55.754
and noted that the GOP assault
on voting rights

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:58.323
is the most ferocious attack
on democracy

00:10:58.323 --> 00:10:59.825
since the era of Jim Crow.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:04.163
-We are witnessing right now a
massive and unabashed assault

00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:05.664
on voting rights

00:11:05.664 --> 00:11:09.869
unlike anything we've ever seen
since the Jim Crow era.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.777
This is Jim Crow in new clothes.

00:11:17.777 --> 00:11:19.611
-He's right. And the clothes
aren't even good.

00:11:19.611 --> 00:11:20.913
I mean, look at this.

00:11:20.913 --> 00:11:22.581
It looks like he was thrown
naked in the dumpster

00:11:22.581 --> 00:11:24.082
behind a Palm Beach pro shop

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:26.084
and given five minutes
to pick an outfit.

00:11:26.084 --> 00:11:27.419
It's a good Halloween costume

00:11:27.419 --> 00:11:30.222
if you want to go as
"lost grandpa at Disney World."

00:11:30.222 --> 00:11:32.224
Warnock was on the floor
specifically to call for

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:33.959
Senate passage of HR 1,

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:36.094
a sweeping package
of urgent voting reforms

00:11:36.094 --> 00:11:38.597
passed by the House that are
desperately needed

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:41.433
to level what is currently
a very lopsided playing field.

00:11:41.433 --> 00:11:43.168
HR 1 would combat
virtually every

00:11:43.168 --> 00:11:45.938
GOP voter suppression tactic
by, among other things,

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:48.006
mandating nationwide
early voting

00:11:48.006 --> 00:11:49.675
and no-excuse mail voting,

00:11:49.675 --> 00:11:53.178
instituting automatic and
same-day voter registration,

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:56.048
implementing public financing
of elections, and banning

00:11:56.048 --> 00:11:58.383
congressional gerrymandering,
among other things.

00:11:58.383 --> 00:12:00.385
It's also incredibly popular
in polls,

00:12:00.385 --> 00:12:02.221
even among a majority
of Republican voters.

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:04.089
So, naturally,
Republican politicians

00:12:04.089 --> 00:12:05.557
are losing their minds over it.

00:12:05.557 --> 00:12:08.494
House GOP Whip Steve Scalise
began a tweet about the bill

00:12:08.494 --> 00:12:09.828
early this month by writing,

00:12:09.828 --> 00:12:11.664
"Every American should be
outraged by this."

00:12:11.664 --> 00:12:14.799
Oh, I wonder what it's gonna be.
Rising poverty? Child hunger?

00:12:14.799 --> 00:12:16.468
Surprise medical bills?
I can't wait to find out.

00:12:16.468 --> 00:12:17.837
Let's read the rest
of the tweet.

00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:26.779
Wait, that's what you want us
to be outraged about?

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:28.947
A bill that makes it easier
to vote,

00:12:28.947 --> 00:12:31.149
that's also incredibly popular?
You can't start a tweet

00:12:31.149 --> 00:12:33.151
like that and then finish
with something so underwhelming.

00:12:33.151 --> 00:12:35.287
It is like getting up
on a chair in the middle of your

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:37.456
office with a bullhorn and
screaming, "Attention, everyone!

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:39.925
There is a shocking scandal
in this office!

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:41.860
I would like the announce
the free pizza

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.329
in the conference room
does not have pepperoni."

00:12:44.329 --> 00:12:46.699
"There's free pizza
in the conference room?"

00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:48.734
"That's not the important part
of the announcement, Steve!

00:12:48.734 --> 00:12:50.903
Steve! Steve, come back!

00:12:50.903 --> 00:12:52.771
There's more!
They also sent cheesecake!"

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:54.373
Now, because the GOP
is stonewalling,

00:12:54.373 --> 00:12:56.709
there's obviously no realistic
way of passing this bill

00:12:56.709 --> 00:12:58.176
in the Senate with 60 votes.

00:12:58.176 --> 00:12:59.712
So in order to make it a law,

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:03.215
Democrats would have to kill or
make changes to the filibuster,

00:13:03.215 --> 00:13:04.249
which is something

00:13:04.249 --> 00:13:06.084
even President Biden says
he now supports.

00:13:06.084 --> 00:13:07.253
And let's just remember,

00:13:07.253 --> 00:13:08.920
the filibuster
as it currently exists

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.923
is itself a relic
of the Jim Crow era.

00:13:10.923 --> 00:13:12.091
It's not in the Constitution,

00:13:12.091 --> 00:13:13.458
and it hasn't always been
like this.

00:13:13.458 --> 00:13:14.793
It's a relatively recent
invention.

00:13:14.793 --> 00:13:16.461
"Mr. Smith Goes to Washington"
would have been

00:13:16.461 --> 00:13:19.265
a lot less dramatic if all
he had to do was send an email

00:13:19.265 --> 00:13:20.599
to the Senate clerk saying,

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:22.101
"I want to block this bill.
Thanks."

00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:23.602
[As Jimmy Stewart]
You old so-and-so!

00:13:23.602 --> 00:13:24.803
[ Bell ringing ]

00:13:24.803 --> 00:13:26.304
Every time I do
my Jimmy Stewart impression,

00:13:26.304 --> 00:13:27.873
an angel gets his wings.
[ Flatulence ]

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:30.042
And then farts a tiny bit.

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:31.377
[ Laughter ]

00:13:31.377 --> 00:13:33.712
But Republicans are so terrified
of even the prospect

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:35.213
of modifying
the filibuster rules

00:13:35.213 --> 00:13:37.549
that allow them to veto
popular legislation.

00:13:37.549 --> 00:13:39.984
So McConnell took to
the Senate floor on Tuesday

00:13:39.984 --> 00:13:42.087
to make a series of threats
about what would happen

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:43.922
if Democrats
reform the filibuster.

00:13:43.922 --> 00:13:46.859
-Let me say this very clearly

00:13:46.859 --> 00:13:50.362
for all 99 of my colleagues.

00:13:50.362 --> 00:13:55.366
Nobody serving in this chamber
can even begin --

00:13:55.366 --> 00:13:58.837
can even begin to imagine

00:13:58.837 --> 00:14:03.676
what a completely scorched-earth
Senate would look like.

00:14:03.676 --> 00:14:05.844
We wouldn't just erase
every liberal change

00:14:05.844 --> 00:14:08.180
that hurt the country.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.350
We'd strengthen America with all
kinds of conservative policies,

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:15.287
with zero -- zero input
from the other side.

00:14:15.287 --> 00:14:18.457
-Okay, first of all, we can
imagine a scorched-earth Senate.

00:14:18.457 --> 00:14:19.825
It's scorched.

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:22.161
You've done more scorching
than a motel room iron.

00:14:22.161 --> 00:14:24.162
You can't do any more scorching.
The Senate at this point

00:14:24.162 --> 00:14:26.632
is like an Italian restaurant
in New Jersey

00:14:26.632 --> 00:14:29.301
after the Real Housewives
film a scene there.

00:14:29.301 --> 00:14:31.637
There's ziti on the walls,
tables have been flipped over,

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:33.138
all the wine glasses
are smashed.

00:14:33.138 --> 00:14:34.773
Also, you're the one
who scorched it.

00:14:34.773 --> 00:14:37.609
You already nuked the filibuster
for Supreme Court nominees.

00:14:37.609 --> 00:14:40.312
You bragged during
Barack Obama's presidency

00:14:40.312 --> 00:14:41.980
that you would grind
the institution to a halt

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:44.750
to sabotage his agenda.
You rushed to confirm

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.585
a Supreme Court nominee
before the election

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:49.021
with no support from Democrats
in just 30 days.

00:14:49.021 --> 00:14:51.690
And you guys passed a tax bill
along party lines

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.425
in the dead of night
after scribbling changes

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:55.194
in the margins
at the last minute

00:14:55.194 --> 00:14:57.496
like you were making notes
on a friend's screenplay.

00:14:57.496 --> 00:14:59.330
I would focus less on
the soundtrack and more on

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.566
character development.

00:15:00.566 --> 00:15:02.267
And also, the bad guy
should get away with it.

00:15:02.267 --> 00:15:04.069
Republicans tried to steal
the last election

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:05.404
through the courts.
That didn't work.

00:15:05.404 --> 00:15:07.238
So now they're trying to steal
the next election

00:15:07.238 --> 00:15:08.573
through voter suppression.

00:15:08.573 --> 00:15:11.009
Nuking or changing
the filibuster to stop them

00:15:11.009 --> 00:15:12.177
is a moral necessity.

00:15:12.177 --> 00:15:14.079
We badly need sweeping reforms

00:15:14.079 --> 00:15:16.081
to make our democracy
a level playing field.

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:19.285
Make it easy for everyone to
vote in person or by mail.

00:15:19.285 --> 00:15:21.086
And make sure
it remains legal to...

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:22.587
-Bring Grandma some water.

00:15:22.587 --> 00:15:24.256
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:28.159
♪♪

00:15:28.159 --> 00:15:29.694
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:15:29.694 --> 00:15:32.131
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:35.133
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:15:35.133 --> 00:15:36.634
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:15:36.634 --> 00:15:38.870
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.373
Stay safe, wear a mask,
get vaccinated.

00:15:41.373 --> 00:15:42.408
We love you.

